---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site';
---

<Base
  title="Acceptable use"
  description="What you may and may not do on acqi.tech, and with preview access."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="micro micro--red mb-1">Legal</p>
      <h1>Acceptable use policy</h1>
      <div class="article-head__meta">
        <span class="micro">Last updated 17 November 2026</span>
        <span class="micro">Part of the terms of use</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy applies to the public site and to preview access. It is short because it
          covers a small surface. Breach of it is a breach of the
          <a href="/legal/terms/">terms of use</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not attack the site</h2>
        <p>
          Do not probe, scan, overload, or attempt to bypass authentication except as part of a
          coordinated disclosure under the process on the <a href="/security/">security page</a>.
          If you find a vulnerability, report it to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a> rather than
          demonstrating it against live traffic.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not scrape or mirror</h2>
        <p>
          Automated bulk retrieval of pages, wholesale copying of site content, and republishing
          under another brand are not permitted. Ordinary search engine indexing of public pages
          is permitted. The preview is excluded from indexing and must stay that way.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not share preview credentials</h2>
        <p>
          Preview access is issued to named individuals. Do not post the password publicly, do
          not include it in a document that circulates beyond the recipient, and do not use the
          preview to demonstrate a working product to a third party. If a colleague needs access,
          ask us and they will be given their own.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not put confidential data in the contact form</h2>
        <p>
          Describe a situation, not a data set. Do not submit target inventories, credentials,
          personal data about third parties, or anything you would not send over ordinary email.
          If we need sensitive material, we will set up an appropriate channel first.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not misrepresent the product</h2>
        <p>
          Do not use material from this site to state that a certification is held, that a
          customer uses the product, or that a capability is generally available when the site
          says it is planned or partial. The <a href="/status/">status page</a> is the reference.
        </p>

        <h2>Do not use the site unlawfully</h2>
        <p>
          No unlawful purpose, no infringement of another party's rights, no attempt to interfere
          with another person's use of the site, and no automated submission of the contact form.
        </p>

        <h2>Consequences</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend preview access or block traffic where this policy is breached. Where the
          breach is a genuine security report made in good faith, we will not take action against
          the reporter, and we will say so in writing if asked.
        </p>

        <h2>Reporting</h2>
        <p>
          Report abuse or a suspected breach to
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.securityEmail}`}>{SITE.securityEmail}</a>. We acknowledge within
          two working days.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
